//- 1:15 WORDS THAT DON'T TRANSLATE, then 2:30 REDHEADS. The first evidence for the thesis: if color were out in the world, languages would agree on where each one starts and stops.

//- Paint chips: the colour, its word, and what the other language needs to say it. Eight a slide, four by two. The hex values are guesses, in scss/talk/_swatches.scss.
section.swatches(data-timing="30")
  h2 Only in Spanish
  dl
    .celeste
      dt(lang="es") celeste
      dd sky blue
    .trigueno
      dt(lang="es") trigueño
      dd the color of wheat
    .zarco
      dt(lang="es") zarco
      dd pale blue eyes
    .moreno
      dt(lang="es") moreno
      dd tanned or brunette
    .canoso
      dt(lang="es") canoso
      dd going gray
    .bermejo
      dt(lang="es") bermejo
      dd strawberry blond
    .pardo
      dt(lang="es") pardo
      dd grayish brown
    .amoratado
      dt(lang="es") amoratado
      dd bruise purple
  aside.notes
    ul
      li Evidence: if color were out in the world, languages would agree on where each one starts and stops.
      li Colors of particular things: skin, eyes, hair, sky. English needs a phrase for every one.
      li Read three or four. The rest make the point by being there.
      li Moreno is what everyone on the beach out there is trying to get.
      li Bermejo was Spanish's main word for red until rojo took over in the 15th century. Hold that for the redheads.
      li Pardo: Spanish says every cat at night is pardo. English says they're all gray.
      li Unverified: check every word with a native speaker from Spain before it ships.

section.swatches(data-timing="30")
  h2 Only in English
  dl
    .teal
      dt teal
      dd(lang="es") verde azulado
    .hazel
      dt hazel
      dd(lang="es") color avellana
    .auburn
      dt auburn
      dd(lang="es") castaño rojizo
    .navy
      dt navy
      dd(lang="es") azul marino
    .taupe
      dt taupe
      dd(lang="es") gris topo
    .eggshell
      dt eggshell
      dd(lang="es") blanco cáscara de huevo
    .periwinkle
      dt periwinkle
      dd(lang="es") azul pervinca
    .puce
      dt puce
      dd(lang="es") color pulga
  aside.notes
    ul
      li Spanish needs two words for every one of these. Eggshell takes four.
      li Taupe is French for mole, and topo is Spanish for mole. Puce is French for flea, and half the English speakers here don't know it either.
      li Unverified, azul pervinca and color pulga most of all.

